    {
      "sentence_id": 11,
      "text": "1 3.After some arguments, learned counsel for the applicant has made a statement at the Bar, on instructions, that he does not want to press other prayers made in the instant application and states that the applicant is ready to appear before the court below and seek his bail and that his release be considered in view of law laid down by Hon'ble Apex Court in the case of Satender Kumar Antil Vs.\nCentral Bureau of Investigation and another reported in (2022) 10 SCC 51.\n4.Per contra, learned AGA states that he has no objection to the aforesaid prayer made by learned counsel for the applicant for not pressing the other prayers made in the instant application.",
      "rhetorical_role": "PREAMBLE",
      "start": 1176,
      "end": 1841,
      "entities": [
        {
          "text": "Apex Court",
          "label": "COURT",
          "start": 1525,
          "end": 1535
        },
        {
          "text": "Satender Kumar Antil Vs.\nCentral Bureau of Investigation and another reported in (2022) 10 SCC 51",
          "label": "PRECEDENT",
          "start": 1551,
          "end": 1648
        }
      ],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "PREAMBLE"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 12,
      "text": "5.In view of the above, in case the applicant appears before the court below within three weeks from today and seeks bail, his release be considered in view of law laid down by Hon'ble Apex Court in the case of Satender Kumar Antil Vs. Central Bureau of Investigation and another reported in (2022) 10 SCC 51.\n6.With the aforesaid observations, this application under Section 482 Cr.P.C. is finally disposed off.",
      "rhetorical_role": "PREAMBLE",
